<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Lupus I of Aquitaine</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">fl. c. 670s</span> · <a href="/centuries/7th-century">7th century</a> · Also known as Lupus I, Duke of Gascony</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Lupus was a duke in south-western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gaul">Gaul</a> in the 670s, recorded as ruling Aquitaine and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gascony">Gascony</a> on behalf of the Merovingian kings while acting with growing independence. He presided over a church council in the region and is said to have tried to seize <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/limoges">Limoges</a>. He is one of the first known leaders of the virtually independent duchy of Aquitaine, before <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/odo-the-great">Odo the Great</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/lupus-i-of-aquitaine.jpg" alt="Lupus I of Aquitaine" width="320" height="297" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Paul Vidal de La Blache · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Frankish_kingdoms_in_628.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
